# Trivy ignore list for the weekly Security scan (issue #21). Every entry
# below is verified upstream-blocked as of 2026-08-23 — not fixable by a
# change in this repo. Do not add a CVE here without the same verification:
# confirm which artifact it lives in and that no newer upstream release
# carries the fix.
#
# Revisit policy: re-check this list whenever gh or npm ship a new release.
# Re-run `trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL ghcr.io/calandria-dev/calandria:latest`
# WITHOUT --ignorefile and prune any entry that no longer appears. A CVE that
# isn't in this file will still fail the weekly scan — that's intentional;
# keeping this list to exactly what's confirmed unfixable is what makes a red
# run meaningful again.
#
# NOT listed here on purpose (verified fixed upstream, just needed a rebuild):
# the golang stdlib + x/net-vendored-in-stdlib CVEs that were baked into the
# gh 2.97.0 that shipped in the image at the time this file was written
# (CVE-2026-33818, CVE-2026-56853, CVE-2026-56858, CVE-2026-56859,
# CVE-2026-56860, CVE-2026-56862, CVE-2026-39821, CVE-2026-46600). gh 2.98.0
# is already built with go1.26.7 (>= the 1.26.6 fix for all eight). A first
# rebuild attempt still shipped 2.97.0 despite that — Docker's layer cache
# keys on the `apt-get install gh` command's *text*, not on what apt actually
# resolves, so an unpinned install silently kept the stale cached layer. The
# Dockerfile now pins `gh=2.98.0` explicitly for this reason; bumping that
# pin (see the comment there) is how gh updates happen going forward, and how
# a rebuild is guaranteed to actually change the layer. Confirmed the fix
# itself by downloading gh_2.98.0_amd64.deb from cli.github.com and checking
# `strings usr/bin/gh` for the embedded go1.26.7 buildinfo string. 2026-08-23.

# --- golang.org/x/mod, compiled into /usr/bin/gh ---
# cli/cli's own go.mod pins x/mod v0.38.0; the fix ships in v0.40.0. This is
# a real dependency bump in cli/cli's code, independent of the Go toolchain
# version above — confirmed still v0.38.0 in gh's latest release (v2.98.0,
# 2026-08-20) by downloading the .deb and grepping the binary for the
# embedded module path/version string.
# Watch: https://github.com/cli/cli/releases — look for a release whose
# go.mod reaches golang.org/x/mod v0.40.0 or later.
# Verified 2026-08-23.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# --- npm's own vendored node_modules, bundled inside npm 12.0.2 ---
# npm 12.0.2 is npm's newest release (`npm view npm dist-tags` — no dist-tag,
# including `next-12`, points past 12.0.2), and it vendors brace-expansion
# 5.0.7, tar 7.5.19, and ip-address 10.2.0 in its own bundled node_modules.
# None of this is Calandria's dependency tree: package-lock.json already
# resolves the app's own ip-address to 10.4.0 (above the 10.3.1 fix for
# CVE-2026-69192, confirmed via `npm ls ip-address --all`), so the
# ip-address hit below is npm's bundled copy, not ours.
# Watch: https://www.npmjs.com/package/npm — a release past 12.0.2.
# Verified 2026-08-23.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-73566
CVE-2026-69192
